# fenrirealm-monitor — runtime configuration
#
# The Go binary reads NO environment variables at runtime: everything is
# CLI flags on cmd/monitor. This file documents the deployment-facing
# knobs; nothing here is sourced automatically — translate them into the
# compose/Dokploy service definition (or a wrapper script) instead.
#
# Ingest contract (see fenrirealm-backend docs/architecture/subsystems/monitoring.md):
#   POST /ingest/{project}/sentry|profile|error|xhprof
#   POST /api/{project}/store|envelope        (Sentry SDK compatibility)
#   POST /api/profiler/store                  (spiral-packages/profiler)
#   TCP 9913                                  (Monolog newline-JSON)
#   GET  /up                                  (health check)
#
# Flag             Default     Meaning
# ---------------- ----------- --------------------------------------------------
# -db              monitor.db  SQLite path — mount a PERSISTENT volume; single
#                              instance only (no replicas).
# -http            :8000       UI + Sentry/profile/error/xhprof ingest.
# -socket          :9913       Monolog TCP socket.
# -retention-days  30          Occurrences older than this are pruned in the
#                              background (chunked deletes; issues kept).
# -prune-interval  10m         Retention cycle frequency.
# -cors-origin     (empty)     Browser origin allowed to POST first-party
#                              error/profile reports (e.g. the SvelteKit
#                              client-side reporter). Empty = no CORS.
#
# Example compose command:
#   command: ["/monitor", "-db", "/data/monitor.db", "-http", ":8000", "-socket", ":9913"]
#   volumes:  [monitor-data:/data]
#
# The PRODUCERS live in the client projects, not here — their env keys are
# documented in fenrirealm-backend/.env.example (MONITOR_*, XHPROF_ENABLED,
# PROFILER_ENDPOINT, SENTRY_LARAVEL_DSN) and fenrirealm-front/.env.example.
